  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"I machine-stitched the words away on the cover, leaving the important ones behind, with threads dangling madly everywhere -- a little bit subversive perhaps?  On the inside pages, the words are sealed in place and can't be easily removed or erased; and yet the tracing paper makes it a bit hard to discern what is written. The words are printed on paper where I had also printed an image of the threads off all the covers."--Fiona Dempster, 23 Sandy Gallery website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Book constructed of 100% cotton watercolor paper, archival ink, tracing paper and cotton, and machine stitching with waxed linen thread. Bound by a modified pamphlet stitch, and issued in red Nepalese lokta paper pouch.</subfield>
